                    {
                        "translation_id": "96befba0-0155-431f-b87b-df837d72ff0b",
                        "source_entry_id": "a8ee5c2e-77b8-3f85-a0a8-e3da243c0ff7",
                        "source_sense_id": "40afe0fd-39f9-3c89-a346-5d8f9d489235",
                        "source_sense_description": "Staat in Ostafrika",
                        "target_lang_word": "Djibouti",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Djibouti",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d14da776-5d24-3b6c-bc70-388c09ff13e0",
                                        "entry_id": "d3deeebe-9f78-3a53-837e-3bfdf2fe3df5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A country in East Africa. Official name: Republic of Djibouti."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6d073c6b-1075-40ca-85f5-29737e5f09bc",
                                                "sense_id": "d14da776-5d24-3b6c-bc70-388c09ff13e0",
                                                "text": "The US officials added that that the situation has angered Djiboutian government officials, and that the US military in Djibouti has messaged back to Washington “significant concerns” over keeping the detainees there and the possible impact on military relations."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "15b5d1a7-af0e-3937-9499-37634f9f9847",
                                        "entry_id": "d3deeebe-9f78-3a53-837e-3bfdf2fe3df5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The capital city of Djibouti."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ff34832-f4b5-4944-8428-2c750bffece3",
                                                "sense_id": "15b5d1a7-af0e-3937-9499-37634f9f9847",
                                                "text": "The French have been having a great deal of trouble at Djibouti with a tribe of the interior, the Issas, who are vehemently opposed to the progress of the railway through their country. Throughout the first half of March, raids were incessant on parties in and about the town itself. A detachment of marines was sent out and restored peace, at all events for the moment. In the meantime fifty Hausas from the Ivory Coast are on their way to form a nucleus of a permanent garrison at Djibouti, and their sergeant is no less a person than Koulery the brother of Behanzin late King of Dahomey."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "91d6cf5e-b306-4a5c-86a6-df79cd30b1fa",
                        "source_entry_id": "a8ee5c2e-77b8-3f85-a0a8-e3da243c0ff7",
                        "source_sense_id": "40afe0fd-39f9-3c89-a346-5d8f9d489235",
                        "source_sense_description": "Staat in Ostafrika",
                        "target_lang_word": "Djibouti",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Djibouti",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2ee4f934-a862-332c-be25-883ee30f1f5e",
                                        "entry_id": "8045340d-64ee-3250-88ef-c4cc239605a3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Pays d’Afrique de l’est, bordé par l’Érythrée au nord, la mer Rouge à l’est, la Somalie au sud-est, et l’Éthiopie au sud-ouest."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Pays"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eb38bb35-8222-4631-a9ba-d6004aa42d4d",
                                                "sense_id": "2ee4f934-a862-332c-be25-883ee30f1f5e",
                                                "text": "C’est une question de management plus que de tactique, appuie Julien Mette, ancien sélectionneur de Djibouti."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3de625c9-a486-43ed-bffd-3e2f74477fb3",
                                                "sense_id": "2ee4f934-a862-332c-be25-883ee30f1f5e",
                                                "text": "À Djibouti, nous avons aussi notre propre art martial. Il s’agit du Dakaïto Ryu, un art martial fondé en 1995 par Maître Ô Senseï Looita, originaire de Djibouti."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "61383361-d22c-3e84-a6d3-37db8274aef8",
                                        "entry_id": "8045340d-64ee-3250-88ef-c4cc239605a3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ville de ce pays, qui en est la capitale."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "582593f8-c4b4-461e-b0ae-d8fdd613f63e",
                                                "sense_id": "61383361-d22c-3e84-a6d3-37db8274aef8",
                                                "text": "Quand on veut changer d’air, on peut se diriger vers Lahej, dans les terres ou vers Djibouti."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0c48b5e1-b2ef-457f-b357-1832de4d8fbc",
                                                "sense_id": "61383361-d22c-3e84-a6d3-37db8274aef8",
                                                "text": "17 février 1941. Je dois rejoindre Harrar, en territoire éthiopien, et me mettre en contact avec les patriotes favorables à l’empereur. La meilleur façon d’y arriver reste la voie ferrée qui va de Djibouti à Addis-Abeba, en passant par Dire Dawa. Signé : cap. Koïnsky."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
